{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/telegraf","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.411Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/telegraf/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/telegraf/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Telegraf image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Telegraf?\n\nTelegraf is a server-based agent for collecting and sending all metrics and events from databases, systems, and IoT sensors.\n\nSee: [influxdata.com/time-series-platform/telegraf/](https://www.influxdata.com/time-series-platform/telegraf/)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `1`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to telegraf version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Configuration\n\nTelegraf can be configured using a mix of a config file, environment variables, and CLI options. If you need to get a config file, once your database / output is configured and is running you can use this command to get it using telegraf CLI shipped with the container:\n\n    telegraf config <options> > telegraf.conf\n\nFor more configuration information refer to [Get Started - Configuration](https://docs.influxdata.com/telegraf/v1/get-started/#configure-telegraf))\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start a telegraf instance\n\n    docker run --name telegraf-logging -d mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/telegraf:1\n\nThe default container startup command is `telegraf`.\n\n ### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe telegraf image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/telegraf:1 /bin/bash\n\nIf you have a config file ready, or need access to ports in the container, the following example shows both in action:\n\n    docker run -it -p 8080:8080 --mount type=bind,source=<path to file>/telegraf.conf,target=/telegraf.conf mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/telegraf:1 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:12:14.2602757+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"124K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"1.31","digest":"sha256:ddcff476caba862467024d6db230b4de2a5c1104f43e7426d669adf5dacf4e1a","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:50:25.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1"